&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: verdana, geneva, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;At Woolpert, you’ll do work that matters.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: verdana, geneva, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;As a leading global architecture, engineering, and geospatial firm, we help clients solve complex challenges that shape communities, strengthen critical infrastructure, advance technology, and improve the world around us. Here, you’ll collaborate across disciplines, tackle meaningful projects, and build a career defined by growth, opportunity, and impact.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Position Overview&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Woolpert is seeking a Project Manager to join our growing Transportation Team in Texas. The Project Manager will primarily lead the execution of projects for our Texas clients from proposal through detailed design. Ideal candidates will be self-motivated with a strong technical background to guide staff through projects. The Project Manager may also serve as a subject matter expert in support of other projects across the country and around the world.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-teams=&quot;true&quot;&gt;We are unable to provide visa sponsorship for this position. &amp;nbsp;Applicants must already possess work authorization in the country the job is located.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h5&gt;What you will do:&lt;/h5&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead project teams through the development of preliminary engineering, detailed design, and quantification of transportation projects.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure deliverables and quality standards are met in accordance with the agreed scope, schedule, and budget.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage and support internal and client cross-functional teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Leverage existing relationships and new client and consultant relationships in the pursuit of new work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Actively participate in professional societies, organizations, and conferences by serving on boards, presenting at luncheons or conferences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h5&gt;What you will bring:&lt;/h5&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s Degree in Civil Engineering from an ABET-accredited program preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Active PE License in Texas or ability to obtain a Texas PE license within in one year of hire.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;TXDOT Prequalification’s
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bridge Design&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Multi-Level Interchange Design&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bridge Class Culvert, Non-Bridge Class Culvert and Inlet Design&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Minimum 10 years of experience in bridge design preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Must be able to travel 10-15% to client sites.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of TXDOT Project Development Process, construction documentation &amp;amp; administration and knowledge in state, local municipalities design process is a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;TXDOT precertification’s in TXDOT bridge design/development preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;AutoCAD and Civil3D experience preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong leadership, organization, and communication skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work independently as well as in a collaborative team environment; offer constructive feedback and direction to support goals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Woolpert, Inc. is a cutting-edge national architecture, engineering and geospatial (AEG) firm. &amp;nbsp;Our transportation practice is deeply rooted in the firm’s long history of providing exceptional client service and innovative design. Through our integrated design approach, we provide comprehensive, full-service consulting to turn our client problems and needs into opportunities and successes, blending engineering excellence with progressive technology and geospatial applications. &amp;nbsp;We employ seasoned industry leaders who are willing to share their technical expertise to present viable solutions to our clients. Our Transportation group is rapidly becoming one of the top firms serving ODOT and LPA clients across Ohio. Woolpert is certified as an Employer of Choice by Great Place To Work®. &amp;nbsp;We believe great companies are built from exceptional people and amazing clients.&lt;/p&gt;
