&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: verdana, geneva, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;As a leading global architecture, engineering, and geospatial firm, we help clients solve complex challenges that shape communities, strengthen critical infrastructure, advance technology, and improve the world around us. Here, you’ll collaborate across disciplines, tackle meaningful projects, and build a career defined by growth, opportunity, and impact.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Overview&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Construction Manager Intern will work on-site alongside the Woolpert construction management team working on aviation and/or road and bridge construction projects. Projects could consist of bridge deck overlays or replacements, highway paving, or reconstruction, airport runway or taxiway construction, electrical (nav aids, lighting, conduit, etc.) or, subgrade stabilization – to name a few. All these projects directly impact the communities where we live and work.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We are open to students in the following states: Colorado, Wyoming, Texas, Utah, Indiana or Ohio&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This internship has a significant portion of work onsite/in-office. Woolpert does not provide housing or relocation for internships/co-ops.&lt;br&gt;We are unable to provide visa sponsorship for this position. Applicants must already possess work authorization in the country the job is located.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you will do:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work as a member of an industry leading construction management team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assist construction managers with inspections of construction projects and materials for compliance with applicable codes, standards, and approved construction plans/specifications&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Gain real-world experience by working on actual projects alongside experienced inspectors and construction managers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assist on a variety of projects spanning clients and disciplines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work as a member of a team that coordinates with other internal teams and external subs and clients.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform tasks and solve problems alongside the construction management team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Evaluate, select and apply standard techniques, procedures and criteria&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assists with performing quality control reviews and quality assurance procedures within areas of expertise&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Reviews and interprets construction documents, site drawings, as-built drawings, and specifications&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Produce daily and weekly reports&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Opportunity to work with current technology including, materials testing, drones, pavement profilograph, surveying, pipe inspections and pavement marking reflectomer testing.&lt;/li&gt;
