&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: verdana, geneva, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;As a leading global architecture, engineering, and geospatial firm, we help clients solve complex challenges that shape communities, strengthen critical infrastructure, advance technology, and improve the world around us. Here, you’ll collaborate across disciplines, tackle meaningful projects, and build a career defined by growth, opportunity, and impact.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Position Overview&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Woolpert is hiring an &lt;strong&gt;Engineering&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;strong&gt;Technician&lt;/strong&gt; (&lt;strong&gt;Field/Civil Engineering) &lt;/strong&gt;to join our dynamic Site Civil Team. This position will report to the Engineering Team Leader and will support hybrid or in office in our Fairview Heights, IL/St. Louis Metro office.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are unable to provide visa sponsorship for this position. &amp;nbsp;Applicants must already possess work authorization in the country the job is located.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You Will Do as an Engineering Technician (Field/Civil Engineering) at Woolpert:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and create site layout plans in alignment with client requirements and Woolpert standards.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Utilize AutoCAD Civil 3D to develop concept plans, grading plans, and site designs.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with project management teams to identify impediments and develop/implement solutions to overcome obstacles. &amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform site due diligence assessments and compile data and reports.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform&amp;nbsp;roadway pavement evaluations&amp;nbsp;and compile reports.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform occasional field work, frequent local travel, and overnight travel, as needed. &amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You Will Bring:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Must have an&amp;nbsp;Associates degree&amp;nbsp;or technical certification from a technical school&amp;nbsp;or four (4)&amp;nbsp;years&amp;nbsp;related experience.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in Autodesk Civil 3D. &amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Valid Driver’s License – Clean driving record.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to multi-task, appropriately prioritize workflow, and complete tasks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Must be mentally and physically capable of performing all essential duties required of the position.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Must have above average verbal and written communication skills for both internal and external relationships. &amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Must be able to effectively communicate and present information in one-on-one and small group situations.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Must be able to read and interpret construction drawings and specifications.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Must&amp;nbsp;be able to read,&amp;nbsp;write&amp;nbsp;and interpret reports, business&amp;nbsp;correspondence&amp;nbsp;and procedural documentation.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Must be able to apply mathematical concepts of plane and solid geometry and trigonometry.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Must be able to perform basic mathematical calculations (fractions, percentages, ratios and proportions) and apply to practical situations.  &lt;/li&gt;
