&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Position Overview&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Woolpert is hiring a &lt;strong&gt;Hydrographic Data Processing Specialist&lt;/strong&gt; to join our Hydrographic Survey team in our Port Orchard, WA office or Wasilla, AK.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our team supports complex marine survey projects across the U.S., including hydrographic surveys, geophysical investigations, and marine infrastructure assessments. This role is primarily office-based and focused on transforming raw field data into accurate, defensible deliverables that support engineering design, permitting, and construction.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This position is ideal for someone who enjoys working with large geospatial datasets, developing efficient processing workflows, and producing high-quality technical deliverables.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;We are unable to provide visa sponsorship for this position. Applicants must already possess work authorization in the country where the job is located.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You Will Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; Core Processing Workflow (Primary Role):&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Process multibeam and singlebeam hydrographic data using &lt;strong&gt;QPS Qimera&lt;/strong&gt;, including:&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Data cleaning, refraction correction, and sound velocity application&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Patch test validation and calibration review&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Surface generation and uncertainty analysis&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Review and validate acquisition logs and metadata from &lt;strong&gt;QINSy&lt;/strong&gt; to ensure proper integration into processing workflows&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform side scan sonar processing and interpretation using &lt;strong&gt;SonarWiz&lt;/strong&gt;, including:&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mosaicking and gain normalization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Target identification and classification (e.g., debris, infrastructure, seabed features)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contact selection and reporting&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; Geospatial &amp;amp; Deliverable Development:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Export processed datasets for integration into &lt;strong&gt;AutoCAD Civil 3D&lt;/strong&gt;, including:&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Creation of bathymetric surfaces from high-density point clouds&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Generation of contours, breaklines, and gridded soundings (e.g., 25’ x 25’)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Volume calculations and surface comparisons (existing vs. design or layered surfaces)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prepare plan sheets and figures consistent with project standards (e.g., ODMDS-style deliverables, channel surveys, dredge support)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support production of:&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bathymetric maps and sounding sheets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Side scan sonar mosaics and contact plots&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Cross sections and profile views&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;GIS-compatible datasets and metadata&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; Advanced Data Integration:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Integrate datasets across multiple sensors and platforms:&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Multibeam, singlebeam, side scan sonar, sub-bottom (as applicable)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;GNSS control and positioning data&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Terrestrial or mobile LiDAR for shoreline/structure tie-ins&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assist with seabed characterization workflows, including combining backscatter and side scan interpretation where applicable&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support SLAM-integrated datasets or GNSS-denied workflows (as applicable to project needs)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; Quality Assurance &amp;amp; Workflow Development:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform QA/QC checks to ensure data accuracy, consistency, and compliance with project specifications&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Document processing workflows and maintain reproducibility across projects&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify inefficiencies and contribute to improving internal processing standards&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate with field teams to resolve data gaps, anomalies, or acquisition issues&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;Collaboration &amp;amp; Project Support:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work closely with project managers and technical leads to meet project schedules and deliverable requirements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide input to survey planning and acquisition strategies based on processing needs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support proposal efforts with technical approach language, example deliverables, and production estimates&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You Will Bring:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree in surveying, Geomatics, ocean engineering, geology, geography, spatial science, marine science, or related field&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3 years + of Proficiency in &lt;strong&gt;AutoCAD Civil 3D&lt;/strong&gt; for surface development and plan production&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of hydrographic survey principles and geospatial data workflows&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Detail-oriented mindset with a focus on producing accurate, defensible datasets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to manage multiple datasets and deadlines in a production environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Self-motivated, curious, and adaptable with strong problem-solving skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; Preferred Experience and Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with &lt;strong&gt;QINSy&lt;/strong&gt; (acquisition awareness) and &lt;strong&gt;Qimera&lt;/strong&gt; (processing)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with &lt;strong&gt;SonarWiz&lt;/strong&gt; for side scan sonar processing and interpretation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with:&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bathymetric surface generation and uncertainty evaluation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Side scan mosaicking and contact reporting&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Volume calculations and layered surface analysis&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with:&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Sub-bottom profiler data (CHIRP) and interpretation (a plus)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;GNSS processing (Trimble Business Center or similar)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Global Mapper or GIS platforms&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with LiDAR processing and integration workflows&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong data visualization and deliverable presentation skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; What Success Looks Like in This Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Produces clean, accurate bathymetric surfaces and deliverables with minimal rework&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Efficiently processes multibeam and side scan datasets across varying project types&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understands how field decisions impact processing outcomes (and helps improve both)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contributes to consistent, repeatable workflows across the team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Supports high-quality deliverables similar to those used in federal and coastal projects (e.g., channel surveys, ODMDS, infrastructure assessments)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
