&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Base pay offered may vary depending on job-related knowledge, skills, and experience.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Pay Range&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$87,100&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$108,900 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Find out more about what Woolpert has to offer here:&amp;nbsp; &lt;a href=&quot;http://woolpert.com/about-us/&quot;&gt;http://woolpert.com/about-us/&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Woolpert is an equal-opportunity employer.&lt;/strong&gt; Woolpert is committed to the full inclusion of all individuals. We recruit, train, compensate, and promote regardless of race, religion, color, national origin, sex, disability, age, veteran status, and other protected status as required by applicable law.&amp;nbsp; You may view more about EEO on our website: &lt;a href=&quot;https://woolpert.com/wp-content/uploads/2017/05/Equal-Employment-Opportunity-The-Law.pdf&quot;&gt;Equal-Employment-Opportunity-The-Law.pdf&lt;/a&gt; and &lt;a href=&quot;https://woolpert.com/wp-content/uploads/2017/05/EEO-is-the-Law-Supplement.pdf&quot;&gt;EEO is the Law Poster Supplement&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Applicants who require an accommodation throughout the application and interview process should request this in advance by contacting your Recruiter&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;To all agencies: &lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;Please, no phone calls or emails to any employee of Woolpert or any of our subsidiaries about this requisition. All resumes submitted by search firms/employment agencies to any employee at Woolpert via email, the internet, or in any form and/or method will be deemed the sole property of Woolpert, unless such search firms/employment agencies were engaged by Woolpert&#39;s Talent Acquisition Team for this requisition and a valid agreement is in place. In the event a candidate who was submitted outside of Woolpert&#39;s applicant process is hired, no fee or payment of any kind will be paid.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: verdana, geneva, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;At Woolpert, you’ll do work that matters.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: verdana, geneva, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;As a leading global architecture, engineering, and geospatial firm, we help clients solve complex challenges that shape communities, strengthen critical infrastructure, advance technology, and improve the world around us. Here, you’ll collaborate across disciplines, tackle meaningful projects, and build a career defined by growth, opportunity, and impact.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Woolpert is hiring a&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;Remote Sensing Specialist&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;to join our dynamic Aerial Operations team. This position is responsible&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;for downloading, processing, QA/QC, sensor calibration and reporting of bathymetric lidar, topographic lidar, and aerial imagery sensors. This position can require both domestic and international travel for sensor support and troubleshooting.&amp;nbsp;This is a mid-level position where dedicated individuals&amp;nbsp;with critical thinking and&amp;nbsp;problem-solving&amp;nbsp;skills&amp;nbsp;have&amp;nbsp;the opportunity to&amp;nbsp;excel.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are unable to provide visa sponsorship for this position. &amp;nbsp;Applicants must already possess work authorization in the country the job is located.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Relocation support to Denver, CO can be made available for exceptional candidates.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You Will Do:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Download, process, QA/QC collected bathymetric lidar, topographic lidar, and aerial imagery.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support sensor installation and integration into aircraft.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Facilitate calibration of bathymetric lidar, topographic lidar, and aerial imagery systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Sensor and Equipment Maintenance: Install, operate, maintain, and troubleshoot sensor equipment on the ground and in flight.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support mission planning and execution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure safe and secure use of company equipment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop modern approaches to bathymetric lidar, topographic lidar, aerial imagery processing, QA/QC, and calibration.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide excellent customer service to both internal and external clients.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You Will Bring:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Desire&amp;nbsp;to learn and be involved in a dynamic operational team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understanding of computer hardware.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understanding of Lidar Sensor Suites (Leica/Riegl)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;U.S. citizenship.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Must have valid U.S. passport and be willing to travel to CONUS and OCONUS locations as necessary&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Willingness and ability to undergo pre-employment verification and drug screening.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Willingness to travel 10-20% of the year both CONUS and OCONUS.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Land Survey experience is a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High School Diploma and/or G.E.D. and/or related experience, such as:&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Data Acquisition &amp;amp; Processing: Participate in ground and flight operations efforts as needed, including mission planning, execution, briefing, debriefing, communications, and safety.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensuring proper collection of data for accuracy and quality.&lt;/li&gt;
