&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead structural design efforts for data center, industrial, and advanced manufacturing projects.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform structural analysis and design for steel, reinforced concrete, and foundation systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work closely with architectural, civil, MEP, process, and vendor teams to resolve design and coordination items.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Review and help prepare structural calculations, specifications, drawings, and construction documents.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support QA/QC reviews and assist during construction with submittals, RFIs, field questions, and related items.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You Will Bring:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree in Civil Engineering, Structural Engineering, or a related field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Active Professional Engineer (PE) license required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Minimum of 10 years of structural engineering experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Project experience should include data centers, industrial facilities, manufacturing plants, or similar technically complex projects.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience using structural analysis programs, design tools, and BIM coordination workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong working knowledge of IBC, ASCE 7, ACI 318, and AISC standards&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Structural Engineer (SE) license and/or Master’s degree preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
