&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: verdana, geneva, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;At Woolpert, you’ll do work that matters.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: verdana, geneva, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;As a leading global architecture, engineering, and geospatial firm, we help clients solve complex challenges that shape communities, strengthen critical infrastructure, advance technology, and improve the world around us. Here, you’ll collaborate across disciplines, tackle meaningful projects, and build a career defined by growth, opportunity, and impact.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Job Summary&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Woolpert is seeking a Program Director to support the continued growth of our Water Group. This leadership role is responsible for developing and expanding water resources, stormwater, coastal engineering, groundwater, water supply, and water master planning services throughout Texas while supporting strategic growth initiatives nationally.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Program Director will lead business development efforts, strengthen client relationships, identify new market opportunities, collaborate across disciplines, and help position Woolpert as a trusted advisor to federal, state, and local agencies. This role is instrumental in driving profitable growth and advancing Woolpert&#39;s presence within the water industry.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Applicants must be currently authorized to work in the country where the position is located. Woolpert is unable to provide visa sponsorship for this position.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Essential Functions &amp;amp; Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead business development initiatives to expand Woolpert&#39;s Water practice throughout Texas and support strategic national growth objectives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and maintain strong relationships with municipal, state, federal, and private-sector clients.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify, pursue, and secure new business opportunities in water resources, stormwater, coastal engineering, groundwater, water supply, and water master planning.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with market, practice, and technical leaders to develop and execute growth strategies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mentor, develop, and support high-performing teams while fostering a culture of collaboration and excellence.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead proposal development, client presentations, contract negotiations, and strategic pursuits.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Represent Woolpert at industry conferences, professional organizations, and client-facing events.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Promote the application of innovative technologies and advanced analytical tools to enhance service delivery and client outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the development of thought leadership initiatives and market positioning strategies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work collaboratively across business units to identify opportunities and deliver integrated solutions for clients.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experience&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;12+ years of progressively responsible experience within the water industry.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated success in business development, capture management, and client relationship management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting water-related projects and programs for Texas state and local agencies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to develop strategic growth plans and successfully execute market expansion initiatives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading multidisciplinary teams and collaborating across organizational functions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Knowledge, Skills &amp;amp; Abilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of water resources, stormwater, coastal engineering, groundwater, and water supply markets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication, presentation, and relationship-building skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven leadership, mentoring, and team development capabilities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong negotiation, problem-solving, and strategic planning skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to manage multiple priorities while maintaining focus on client satisfaction and business growth.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to identify emerging industry trends and leverage innovative technologies to create client value.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree in Engineering, Environmental Science, Business Administration, or related field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Professional Engineer (PE) license.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Established relationships with Texas municipal, regional, and state agency clients.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting large-scale water infrastructure, resiliency, flood mitigation, or master planning programs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Recognized industry involvement through professional organizations, conference participation, or thought leadership activities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
